<title>RUSSIA: Russia 588-day bond price 97.19 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 588-day bond price 97.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of a new 588-day tranche of two-year interest-bearing government OFZ bonds maturing in July 1998 was 97.19 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Earlier tranches of the issue closed at 101.15 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		   24008</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  2.45 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		  1.12 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  1.16 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		   97.19 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 97.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		   70.35 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	72.08 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	     588 days</p>
<p>    Next coupon date		Jan 15, 1997</p>
<p>    Coupon rate		     48.54 pct</p>
<p>    Original issue date	   July 17, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   July 15, 1998</p>
<p>Proceeds include accruals.</p>
<p>In money terms, the January 15 coupon amounts to 121,018 roubles, less accruals of 65,164 roubles.</p>
<p>On December 4, the finance ministry will offer 8.50 trillion roubles in six-month GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22061) and repay about 7.08 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22035).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
